User asked: write a program of prime numbers
Agent answered: Here's a JavaScript program to find prime numbers up to a given number:

```javascript
function findPrimeNumbers(n) {
    let primeNumbers = [];
    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        let isPrime = true;
        for (let j = 2; j <= Math.sqrt(i); j++) {
            if (i % j === 0) {
                isPrime = false;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (isPrime) {
            primeNumbers.push(i);
        }
    }
    return primeNumbers;
}

// Example usage:
let n = 50;
let primeNumbers = findPrimeNumbers(n);
console.log(`Prime numbers up to ${n}: ${primeNumbers}`);
```

This program defines a function `findPrimeNumbers(n)` that takes an integer `n` as input and returns an array of prime numbers up to `n`. The function uses a nested loop to check each number up to `n` for primality. If a number is prime, it is added to the `primeNumbers` array. Finally, the program calls the function with an example input `n = 50` and logs the resulting prime numbers to the console.

User asked: wap of bubble sort
Agent answered: Here's a JavaScript program to implement Bubble Sort:

```javascript
function bubbleSort(arr) {
    let n = arr.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (let j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                // Swap arr[j] and arr[j + 1]
                let temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                arr[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return arr;
}

// Example usage:
let arr = [64, 34, 25, 12, 22, 11, 90];
let sortedArr = bubbleSort(arr);
console.log(`Sorted array: ${sortedArr}`);
```

This program defines a function `bubbleSort(arr)` that takes an array `arr` as input and returns the sorted array. The function uses a nested loop to compare each pair of adjacent elements and swap them if they are in the wrong order. This process is repeated until the entire array is sorted. Finally, the program calls the function with an example input array and logs the sorted array to the console.
